; Exports for the Vulkan implicit layer.
;
; A .def file rather than __declspec(dllexport) on the definitions: the Vulkan
; headers already declare vkGetInstanceProcAddr and vkGetDeviceProcAddr without
; dllexport, so redefining them with it is a linkage conflict (C2375). This is
; also the conventional way Khronos' own layers export on Windows.
;
; NAMES, NOT ORDINALS. docs/19_SAFETY_AND_ANTICHEAT.md: the DLL ships with its
; real filename and real exports, because an anti-cheat vendor or a loader log
; must be able to say what this is. Exporting by ordinal to be tidier would be
; a step towards being harder to identify, which CLAUDE.md rule 3 rejects.
LIBRARY FrameLedger.VkLayer
EXPORTS
    vkNegotiateLoaderLayerInterfaceVersion
    vkGetInstanceProcAddr
    vkGetDeviceProcAddr
    FlVkLayerName
    FlVkLayerWouldActivate
    FlVkLayerSelfScanSaysPassthrough
